  "handoff_summary": {
    "completed": "- Added parseFrontmatter(_:) private method to CooklangParser that detects --- frontmatter blocks (skipping leading blank lines), parses scalar key: value entries verbatim, and joins list values (key: followed by indented - item lines) with ', '. Returns (entries, consumed) where consumed is the line count to skip in the main parse loop.\n- Replaced inMetadataRegion / >> logic in parse(_:) with a single parseFrontmatter call; the main loop now iterates over lines[consumed...], so frontmatter delimiters never reach step text.\n- >> lines are now treated as plain step text with no special handling.\n- Build complete with zero compiler errors.",
    "remaining": "Test coverage for: frontmatter with scalars, lists, leading blank lines, unclosed block, >> lines as step text, and files with no frontmatter. Tester agent responsibility.",
    "risks": "Recipes that used >> metadata will silently have those lines appear as step text rather than metadata \u2014 this is intentional per spec but is a breaking change for existing recipe files. Downstream beads or app code that relied on >> metadata keys will need updating.",
    "verdict": "approved",
